## 8. Current Research Extensions

I am continuing to develop KNWM beyond the experiments reported in the ICLR submission.

### 8.1 LLM–KNWM Integration

I have developed an initial AGI-oriented system combining KNWM with an LLM.

In this architecture:

- The LLM primarily handles language input and output.
- KNWM handles knowledge, memory, reasoning, and planning.

The system also includes an initial capability-expansion mechanism.

When an existing capability is insufficient, KNWM can plan a possible solution, guide code development and testing, and retain newly developed capabilities for later use.

### 8.2 3D Perception

I am improving KNWM's ability to obtain structured information from visual observations.

The goal is to connect 3D perception with the existing knowledge-neuron architecture.

This would allow the system to use observed physical states for further reasoning and planning.

### 8.3 Embodied Planning

Another research direction is applying KNWM's existing knowledge-driven planning mechanisms to embodied intelligence.

I am interested in how mathematical and physical knowledge can support planning under changing environmental conditions and safety constraints.

These are ongoing research directions, not claims of completed real-world robotic deployment.

